{
  "note": "Cross-check running-report guard contract (issue #4158). Each case is one worker `running` report against a run row in `status`, in the given `lane`, holding the given `approval` state, and says whether the api accepts it (`expect_applied`). Lanes: gated = plan_cross_check_gated, not auto-approved; required_forced_human = plan_cross_check_required with auto_approve=false; required_auto = plan_cross_check_required with auto_approve=true and an autopilot-stored plan (SetRunAutopilotPlan), reachable only in claimed/running because SetRunAwaitingApproval clears auto_approve on every park, so only the no-approval cases exist; required_auto_parked = a required run that starts with auto_approve=true and parks through the real SetRunAwaitingApproval, which clears auto_approve and so makes it a human-gated row (the forced-human behaviour: running refused without an applied approval bound to the current gate revision); ordinary = neither. Approvals (approve_plan input): applied_bound_current = applied, not superseded, bound to the current gate revision; unapplied = bound to the current revision but never applied; stale_revision = applied and bound, but to an earlier gate revision than the current one; unbound = applied with no gate binding; superseded = applied and bound to the current revision but settled disposition=superseded; none = no approve_plan input. `payload_mismatch` means the stored plan_md differs from the plan in the presented gate payload. A plan_md is stored in EVERY case (the pre-plan running report, which is admitted whatever the lane, is deliberately not covered). Expectations come from api/internal/store/queries/runtime.sql SetRunRunning (the status-independent cross-check clause and the awaiting_approval arm) and migration 00394's trigger, and are asserted against that SQL by api/internal/store/plan_cross_check_running_guard_livedb_test.go. On the agent side agent/test/fake-api-cross-check-running.test.ts asserts every case against the pure rule (crossCheckRunningAdmitted); the fake's /state route is asserted against all of them with FakeApi.modelCrossCheckRunningRule and FakeApi.modelOrdinaryRunningRule on (both off by default, so the route stays accept-all for tests that do not opt in). Do not add an -update flag on either side.",
